   "notes": [
    "Confusion matrix (seaborn-style heatmap, colour map white to dark blue, colour bar 0-25 on the right with ticks 0, 5, 10, 15, 20, 25): 9 rows x 7 columns, a count printed in every cell. Rows = 'Blinded Human Validation' (label printed vertically on the left): A, B, C, D, E, 2OP, EOP, NOP, Error. Columns = 'GPT-3.5 Extracted Option from LLM Textual Response' (printed in bold above the matrix; it is both the figure's title and the column axis title): A, B, C, D, E, GPT: Require Evaluation, Parsing Failed (labels above the columns, slanted).",
    "One row per cell, in reading order (row by row): category = the row label, series = the column label, value = the printed count (source 'printed', label_printed as printed). 63 cells, 51 of them 0.",
    "Cross-checks: the colour of every cell, read against the colour bar (calibrated on its six ticks, residual <= 0.02), gives the printed count within 0.1 for all 63 cells. The counts sum to 100.",
    "Not data: the 5 x 5 block A-E x A-E is outlined cell by cell in pink (the cells where an option was extracted); the two right-hand columns and the four bottom rows have no cell borders."
   ]
