 "uncertain": [
  "Convention: kind 'heatmap', as CONVENTIONS states it: category = the row label (the human-validated class, left), series = the column label (the option GPT-3.5 extracted, top), value = the printed count. A prediction with rows and columns swapped pairs only the cells whose row and column label both occur on the other axis (the A-E block), and then with the transposed value.",
  "The matrix has no numeric axis: both axes are categorical and axes ranges are null, so the scorer normalises by the span of the truth values, 0 to 25 (the colour bar's range as well). One count off is 0.04 of that span: inside the loose band (0.05), outside the tight one (0.02).",
  "The picture has no caption element in the conversion; the paper's text calls it Supplementary Figure S2, 'Confusion matrix of GPT-3.5 performance in the extraction of selected options from the raw textual response of LLMs' (page 58).",
  "Agreement with the paper's text (page 57): a dataset of 100 answers (the cells sum to 100); 'extracted the correct option in 83% of the cases' (columns A-E hold 83 answers), 'an accuracy of 98.8% for those extractions' (82 of 83 on the diagonal; the one miss is row B, column D), 'the remaining 17%' flagged for manual evaluation (14 in 'GPT: Require Evaluation' + 3 in 'Parsing Failed').",
  "figure.bbox is copied from the picture's prov in document.json (l, t, r, b with a bottom-left origin, as stored there)."
 ]
